# Git Workflow

Git history is part of the project documentation.

## Branches

- Never create branches unless explicitly instructed.
- Respect the current Git workflow.

## Commits

- Never create commits.
- Never generate commit messages automatically.
- Never push changes.
- Never merge branches.

## Changes

- Leave all modifications uncommitted.
- Make small, reviewable changes.
- Minimize unrelated file modifications.
- Never reformat files that were not intentionally edited.

## Safety

- Do not delete files unless explicitly instructed.
- Do not overwrite user changes.